---
description: Avoid decorative headers, subtitles, gradients, and box-shadows in UI
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Decorative UI Chrome

Do not add generic "AI-style" page decoration unless the user explicitly asks for it.

## Do not add

- Section titles like "Search Filters", "Hospital Registry", "Overview"
- Descriptive subtitles under section headers
- Decorative header icons next to titles
- Gradient backgrounds on panels or toolbars
- **Box-shadow on panels, cards, sections, toolbars, or wrappers** — use flat borders only
- Count/meta lines such as "12 hospitals registered" in toolbars

## Box-shadow

- Do not add `box-shadow` to new layout containers, filter panels, table sections, or toolbars
- Prefer `border: 1px solid #d2d2d2` (or existing project border tokens) with `box-shadow: none`
- Do not add shadows to make UI feel "premium" or "elevated"
- Existing global field focus rings and framework defaults are fine — do not add extra decorative shadows on top

## Prefer instead

- Match existing page patterns in the codebase (filters, toolbar, table)
- Use borders only when the user asks or when the surrounding feature already uses them
- Keep toolbars minimal — e.g. a right-aligned action button above the table
- Do not place multiple `type="primary"` buttons in the same page view — use one primary CTA for the main action (usually Add/Create) and `type="default"` for filter actions like Search
- Group related page actions in one toolbar row above the table when Search is moved out of the filter panel; keep Search with Clear inside the filter form by default

## Example

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — decorative chrome
<section className="filter-panel" style={{ boxShadow: '0 1px 4px rgba(...)' }}>
  <header>
    <Icon />
    <h2>Search Filters</h2>
    <p>Refine results by name, location, or contact details</p>
  </header>
  ...
</section>

// ✅ GOOD — functional layout only
<section className="filter-panel">
  <FilterForm />
</section>
<div className="table-toolbar">
  <Button type="primary">Add Hospital</Button>
</div>
<DataTable />
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.filter-panel {
  box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(2, 107, 177, 0.06);
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fbfe 0%, #ffffff 48%);
}

/* ✅ GOOD */
.filter-panel {
  border: 1px solid #d2d2d2;
  border-radius: 10px;
  background: #ffffff;
  box-shadow: none;
}
```
